 the posterior black  The posterior aspect displays a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan pink retracted area  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm well delineated irregular tan pink fibrotic  scarred area and abuts the retracted posterior aspect  and the overlying scar bearing skin  This area contains dense  lobulated fibrous tissue with no discrete masses or lesions grossly appreciated  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink and lobulated  Within the axillary tail  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A J  Entire fibrotic scarred area with the deep closest overlying posterior margin in cassettes A D  and the section containing the metal clip in cassette E  K L  Uninvolved fibrotic lobulated parenchyma  M  Skin papule  N P  Representative sections from axillary tail  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior breast tissue  left   are two irregular tan pink unoriented lobulated portions of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The unoriented specimens are inked black  serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable tan yellow to pink cut surface  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes Q T with the smaller portion in cassettes Q R and the larger portion in cassettes S T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  The unoriented specimen displays a moderate amount of cauterizing artifact along one aspect  and entirely submitted in cassettes U V  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  SAM S  YOO