Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  A FEW TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast core needle biopsies  are 6 soft tan yellow to tan pink fragments of tissue  ranging in size from a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  submitted entirely in cassette A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Dennis William Burke  M D  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Katharine Treadway  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
