Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 04 at 16 59 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma and DCIS present at margins of prior excision  stitch at 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INVOLVING 2 OF 7 BLOCKS AND SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM ALL MARGINS  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  SKIN  LEFT CHEST   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT BREAST SCAR PLAQUE   5 O CLOCK   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 04 at 17 35                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm irregular portion of skin containing a 3 2cm in diameter nipple areolar complex  There is a 3 6cm x 0 2cm linear scar at the inferior aspect of the skin  3 0cm from the nipple  There is a stitch designating 12 o clock present at one edge of the skin ellipse  The posterior surface is covered by a tan pink  smooth glistening thin fascia  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm cavity at the inferior  6 o clock  portion of the specimen with surrounding yellow tan fat necrosis and tan white fibrous tissue  No residual mass is identified  The fibrous tissue abuts both the anterior and posterior margins  The cavity comes to within 0 3cm of the anterior margin and within 0 5cm of the posterior margin  The remainder of the breast is tan white  slightly granular  fibrous tissue and a small amount of yellow tan fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  Cavity with nearest relations to anterior and posterior margins  D  Additional section of superior portion of cavity  E  Representative fibrous tissue from lateral breast  F  Representative fibrous tissue with tan cyst from medial aspect  G  Possible lymph nodes from upper outer quadrant  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left chest old incision   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 2 0cm   with a faint linear possible scar at the center  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes H J  with the tips in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  scar plaque  left breast 5 o clock  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of tan white fibrous tissue and small quantities of fatty tissue  which is submitted in toto as cassette K  Resident  PAUL N  STAATS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN LEFT CHEST  RE EXCISION PART C  SCAR LEFT BREAST PLAQUE   5 00  EXCISION , Positive.
